1
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,260
It's got to be the Mountain. He's the biggest.

2
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:05,650
- He's the strongest. - Bulls are bigger than lions.

3
00:02:05,650 --> 00:02:07,530
Doesn't mean I'd pick a bull in a fight.

4
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:09,690
If the bull had fangs and claws, I would.

5
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:14,460
Right, the Mountain or our man Jaime.

6
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,070
If he ever gets out.

7
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:18,790
Loras Tyrell?

8
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:21,900
Loras Tyrell. He's prettier than the queen.

9
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,450
I don't care about pretty.

10
00:02:23,450 --> 00:02:25,160
He's better with a sword than any of them.

11
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,680
How good could he be?

12
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,520
He's been stabbing Renly Baratheon for years,

13
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,210
and Renly ain't dead.

14
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,980
The horses seem a little spooked to you?

15
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,670
They're horses.

16
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,010
They get spooked by their own shadows.

17
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:52,410
Do you hear that?

18
00:02:54,270 --> 00:02:55,250
No.

19
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:58,060
There's something out there.

20
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:25,640
Oh, you're a right little prick.

21
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,740
You should see your face.

22
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,690
I swear you pissed yourself.

23
00:03:29,950 --> 00:03:32,330
"Oh, who goes there? Ahh!"

24
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:34,240
There is something out there.

25
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,090
Yeah, don't even try me.

26
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:39,050
- Rennick. - Do you think I'm an idiot?

27
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,600
Rennick!

28
00:03:47,970 --> 00:03:51,050
- King in the North! - The King in the North!

29
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,710
Five Lannisters dead for every one of ours.

30
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:16,280
They're dead. Take everything they've got.

31
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:18,070
We've nowhere to keep all these prisoners.

32
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,920
Barely enough food to feed our own.

33
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:23,010
We're not executing prisoners, Lord Bolton.

34
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:24,460
Of course, Your Grace.

35
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:26,860
The officers will be useful.

36
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:30,470
Some of them may be privy to Tywin Lannister's plans.

37
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:31,940
I doubt it.

38
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:34,060
Well, we'll learn soon enough.

39
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:38,160
In my family we say, "A naked man has few secrets.

40
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,870
A flayed man none."

41
00:04:39,990 --> 00:04:42,110
My father outlawed flaying in the north.

42
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:45,260
- We're not in the north. - we're not torturing them.

43
00:04:45,350 --> 00:04:47,120
The high road's very pretty,

44
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:49,910
but you'll have a hard time marching your army down it.

45
00:04:50,210 --> 00:04:52,410
The Lannisters hold prisoners of their own.

46
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:56,110
I won't give them an excuse to abuse my sisters.

47
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,620
No, no, don't! Don't!

48
00:04:58,620 --> 00:04:59,910
Please!

49
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,830
The rot's set in.

50
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:08,600
No, don't! No, don't!

51
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,630
Please, don't!

52
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:13,740
It'll get better. It doesn't even hurt.

53
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:16,670
The rot will spread. If we don't take the foot now--

54
00:05:16,670 --> 00:05:18,060
No, you can't!

55
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:23,780
Ser! Please, ser.

56
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:25,730
- I can't lose-- - You'll die if she does it.

57
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:27,540
I don't want to be a cripple, please.

58
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:30,420
Surely one of our men needs your attention more than this cub.

59
00:05:30,470 --> 00:05:32,900
Your men are not my men, My Lord.

60
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:35,620
Put this in your mouth and lie down. You don't want to watch.

61
00:05:35,630 --> 00:05:38,280
- No! You can't! - Bite on it.

62
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:40,820
It's better than biting your own tongue, believe me.

63
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:17,260
- What's your name? - Talisa.

64
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:19,030
Your last name?

65
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:21,870
You want to know what side my family fights on?

66
00:06:21,870 --> 00:06:23,940
You know my family name. You have me at a disadvantage.

67
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:26,960
That boy lost his foot on your orders.

68
00:06:27,730 --> 00:06:29,520
They killed my father.

69
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:32,040
- That boy did? - The family he fights for.

70
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,420
Do you think he's friends with King Joffrey?

71
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:37,670
He's a fisherman's son that grew up near Lannisport.

72
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:38,850
He probably never held a spear

73
00:06:38,850 --> 00:06:40,940
before they shoved one in his hands a few months ago.

74
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:42,690
I have no hatred for the lad.

75
00:06:44,910 --> 00:06:47,200
That should help his foot grow back.

76
00:06:50,790 --> 00:06:53,390
You'd have us surrender, end all this bloodshed.

77
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:56,500
I understand. The country would be at peace

78
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,970
and life would be just

79
00:06:57,970 --> 00:06:59,980
under the righteous hand of good King Joffrey.

80
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:02,690
- You're going to kill Joffrey? - If the gods give me strength.

81
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:05,310
- And then what? - I don't know.

82
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:08,100
We'll go back to Winterfell.

83
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:10,710
I have no desire to sit on the Iron Throne.

84
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,560
So who will?

85
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:14,460
I don't know.

86
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:17,020
You're fighting to overthrow a king,

87
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,770
and yet you have no plan for what comes after?

88
00:07:18,770 --> 00:07:20,580
First we have to win the war.

89
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:28,290
You never told me where you're from.

90
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:30,890
- Volantis. - Volantis?

91
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:32,340
You're far from home.

92
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,600
The boy was lucky you were here.

93
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:37,860
He was unlucky that you were.

94
00:07:47,370 --> 00:07:50,270
You're here to answer for your brother's latest treasons.

95
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,870
Your Grace,

96
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:55,200
whatever my traitor brother has done, I had no part.

97
00:07:55,210 --> 00:07:56,650
You know that. I beg you...

98
00:07:56,650 --> 00:07:58,710
Ser Lancel, tell her of this outrage.

99
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:00,280
Using some vile sorcery,

100
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:03,760
your brother fell on Stafford Lannister with an army of wolves.

101
00:08:03,890 --> 00:08:06,390
Thousands of good men were butchered.

102
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:07,790
After the slaughter,

103
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:10,960
the northmen feasted on the flesh of the slain.

104
00:08:12,570 --> 00:08:15,550
Killing you would send your brother a message.

105
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,750
But my mother insists on keeping you alive.

106
00:08:21,770 --> 00:08:23,180
Stand.

107
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:28,290
So we'll have to send your brother a message some other way.

108
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,080
Meryn.

109
00:08:35,490 --> 00:08:36,700
Leave her face.

110
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:39,100
I like her pretty.

111
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:48,260
Meryn, My Lady is overdressed.

112
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,620
Unburden her.

113
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:58,640
If you want Robb Stark to hear us,

114
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,120
we're going to have to speak louder.

115
00:09:02,610 --> 00:09:04,490
What is the meaning of this?

116
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:15,900
What kind of knight beats a helpless girl?

117
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:18,090
The kind who serves his king, Imp.

118
00:09:18,090 --> 00:09:19,570
Careful, now. We don't want

119
00:09:19,570 --> 00:09:21,810
to get blood all over your pretty white cloak.

120
00:09:21,810 --> 00:09:24,230
Someone get the girl something to cover herself with.

121
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:26,590
She is to be your queen.

122
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,520
Have you no regard for her honor?

123
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:30,810
- I'm punishing her. - For what crimes?

124
00:09:30,810 --> 00:09:33,120
She did not fight her brother's battle, you half-wit.

125
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,500
You can't talk to me like that.

126
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,340
The king can do as he likes!

127
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:38,670
The Mad King did as he liked.

128
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:41,720
Has your uncle Jaime ever told you what happened to him?

129
00:09:41,730 --> 00:09:45,030
No one threatens His Grace in the presence of the kingsguard.

130
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:46,890
I'm not threatening the king, ser.

131
00:09:46,890 --> 00:09:48,690
I am educating my nephew.

132
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:52,330
Bronn, the next time Ser Meryn speaks, kill him.

133
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:56,640
That was a threat. See the difference?

134
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,940
I apologize for my nephew's behavior.

135
00:10:23,270 --> 00:10:26,600
Tell me the truth. Do you want an end to this engagement?

136
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:30,300
I am loyal to King Joffrey, my one true love.

137
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:38,840
Lady Stark, you may survive us yet.

138
00:10:42,890 --> 00:10:44,850
The little king's backed up.

139
00:10:45,110 --> 00:10:47,440
Clogged from balls to brains.

140
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:50,670
You think dipping his wick will cure what ails him?

141
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,810
There's no cure for being a cunt.

142
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,640
But the boy's at that age.

143
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:59,340
And he's got nothing to do all day but pick wings off flies.

144
00:10:59,610 --> 00:11:02,020
Couldn't hurt to get some of the poison out.

145
00:11:10,150 --> 00:11:11,870
What are you doing here, dog?

146
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:14,120
Your uncle left your nameday present

147
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:16,650
and asked me to see that you got it.

148
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,540
And?

149
00:11:21,530 --> 00:11:22,760
What is it?

150
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:25,730
Look inside, Your Grace.

151
00:11:32,110 --> 00:11:33,600
Your Grace.

152
00:11:34,670 --> 00:11:37,920
- Happy nameday, Your Grace. - My nameday has passed.

153
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:40,060
We won't tell if you won't.

154
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:44,820
No.

155
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,640
Her.

156
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:51,440
Touch her.

157
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:15,250
Could you hit her?

158
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,120
My uncle sent you?

159
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,410
Yes, Your Grace.

160
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:34,150
He chose us himself.

161
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:45,920
Use this.

162
00:12:59,490 --> 00:13:00,740
Harder.

163
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:09,080
I said harder.

164
00:13:11,210 --> 00:13:13,540
He'd want me to get his money's worth.

165
00:13:56,940 --> 00:14:00,980
Your Grace, too much pain will spoil the pleasure.

166
00:14:02,690 --> 00:14:04,620
Please, please.

167
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:11,680
Please, Your Grace.

168
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:14,770
Your Grace, if your uncle finds out...

169
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,740
Oh, I want him to find out.

170
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:20,420
You will bring her to his chambers when you're finished

171
00:14:20,430 --> 00:14:22,670
and show him what you've done.

172
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:26,020
Or the same thing will happen to you.

173
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:33,820
Begin.

174
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,190
Harder!

175
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:59,300
Well, if it isn't my favorite whoremonger.

176
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,800
Pray I haven't kept you waiting long.

177
00:15:04,690 --> 00:15:06,080
Your Grace.

178
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:12,870
Now you do the Lannisters' bidding, is that it?

179
00:15:13,630 --> 00:15:16,630
Tell me, was my brother's body even cold

180
00:15:16,630 --> 00:15:19,050
before you secured your newest patron?

181
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,200
I'm a practical man.

182
00:15:22,690 --> 00:15:24,320
Just not a loyal one.

183
00:15:24,530 --> 00:15:26,690
And who would you have me be loyal to?

184
00:15:26,690 --> 00:15:28,480
Your brother's corpse?

185
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:33,100
I don't like you, Lord Baelish.

186
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:36,020
I don't like your face.

187
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:39,600
I don't like the words that come oozing out of your mouth.

188
00:15:40,150 --> 00:15:43,090
I don't want you in my tent one minute more than necessary.

189
00:15:43,090 --> 00:15:45,430
So tell me, why are you here?

190
00:15:47,410 --> 00:15:48,930
You can trust Brienne.

191
00:15:49,190 --> 00:15:51,500
Her loyalty comes without charge.

192
00:15:54,390 --> 00:15:56,860
You still have many friends at court, Your Grace,

193
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,800
many who believe Ned Stark erred by not supporting your claim.

194
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:05,350
Now I understand.

195
00:16:06,630 --> 00:16:08,340
You know I have the numbers.

196
00:16:08,730 --> 00:16:11,170
You know I'm marching on King's Landing.

197
00:16:11,810 --> 00:16:15,150
When I take the throne, you hope to retain your position.

198
00:16:16,590 --> 00:16:18,050
And your head.

199
00:16:18,190 --> 00:16:20,480
I would give priority to my head.

200
00:16:21,370 --> 00:16:23,080
I understand that you don't like me,

201
00:16:23,090 --> 00:16:26,040
and while that saddens me greatly,

202
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:28,660
I did not come here today seeking your affection.

203
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:32,150
When you march on King's Landing,

204
00:16:32,150 --> 00:16:35,850
you may find yourself facing a protracted siege or...

205
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,680
open gates.

206
00:16:56,780 --> 00:16:58,120
Your Grace.

207
00:16:58,420 --> 00:16:59,850
Lord Baelish.

208
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:04,360
All of these tents look the same to me.

209
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,780
- Would you be so kind... - It would be my pleasure.

210
00:17:07,150 --> 00:17:09,520
It took me weeks to learn my way around the camp.

211
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:12,600
Twice I walked in on officers in stages of undress.

212
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:15,330
And the moment I learn which tent is mine,

213
00:17:15,790 --> 00:17:17,230
we're on the move again.

214
00:17:17,230 --> 00:17:18,580
Your tent?

215
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:21,350
Not our tent?

216
00:17:22,170 --> 00:17:23,640
The king snores, perhaps?

217
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:26,550
Or simply prefers solitude?

218
00:17:27,090 --> 00:17:29,790
Pressures of command, no doubt.

219
00:17:29,890 --> 00:17:32,520
Four kings vying for the throne.

220
00:17:32,650 --> 00:17:34,450
I am not tutored in warfare,

221
00:17:34,450 --> 00:17:38,510
but basic arithmetic favors the side with the greater numbers.

222
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:42,750
If war were arithmetic, the mathematicians would rule the world.

223
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:46,630
I did notice your brother entering His Grace's tent just now.

224
00:17:46,630 --> 00:17:48,820
The place of a kingsguard is by the king's side.

225
00:17:48,820 --> 00:17:50,740
And on the night of the your wedding,

226
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:53,470
who was by the king's side then?

227
00:17:53,470 --> 00:17:55,770
You seem quite interested in our marriage.

228
00:17:55,770 --> 00:17:57,810
Your marriage is quite interesting...

229
00:17:58,420 --> 00:18:01,350
Not only to me, but to the realm.

230
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:06,240
The marriage of a wealthy girl always breeds interest, if nothing else.

231
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,130
You've never married, have you?

232
00:18:09,530 --> 00:18:13,720
I've been unlucky in my affections, sadly.

233
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:15,880
That is sad.

234
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,590
Though perhaps it's for the best.

235
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:19,880
The whole notion of marriage seems to confuse you,

236
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:21,730
so allow me to explain.

237
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:23,190
My husband is my king,

238
00:18:23,190 --> 00:18:25,470
and my king is my husband.

239
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:29,860
Here is your tent, Lord Baelish. Good night.

240
00:19:25,370 --> 00:19:27,090
What do you know of this place?

241
00:19:27,590 --> 00:19:29,500
Only that the desert around their walls

242
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:31,810
is called the Garden of Bones.

243
00:19:33,190 --> 00:19:36,190
Every time the Qartheen shut their gates on a traveler,

244
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:38,130
the Garden grows.

245
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:54,030
Go on! You, keep moving!

246
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:03,210
Bring her about!

247
00:20:03,210 --> 00:20:05,070
What kind of fire melts stone?

248
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:08,170
Dragon fire.

249
00:20:08,870 --> 00:20:10,290
There's dragons here?

250
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:12,150
No, all the dragons are dead.

251
00:20:13,730 --> 00:20:15,130
What's that smell?

252
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,110
Dead people.

253
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,700
Move.

254
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:33,210
Please, please, no, no!

255
00:20:39,170 --> 00:20:40,660
No.

256
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:53,020
He's dead.

257
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:56,980
He was my son.

258
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:02,020
My sister was three days ago.

259
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:05,320
My husband, the day before that.

260
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:08,360
They take someone every day?

261
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:12,750
Does anyone live?

262
00:21:36,830 --> 00:21:37,970
Joffrey.

263
00:21:39,310 --> 00:21:40,470
Cersei.

264
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:42,570
Ilyn Payne.

265
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:44,270
The Hound.

266
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:46,240
Joffrey.

267
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:48,640
Cersei.

268
00:21:50,110 --> 00:21:51,310
Ilyn Payne.

269
00:21:52,130 --> 00:21:53,380
The Hound.

270
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:55,240
Joffrey.

271
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:56,870
Cersei.

272
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,280
Ilyn Payne.

273
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:00,130
The Hound.

274
00:22:04,390 --> 00:22:05,740
How dare you?

275
00:22:05,740 --> 00:22:07,800
You may have heard false reports.

276
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:09,570
You betrayed Ned.

277
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:11,940
Betrayed? I wanted him to serve as Protector of The Realm.

278
00:22:11,950 --> 00:22:13,650
I begged him to seize the moment.

279
00:22:13,650 --> 00:22:17,730
I trusted you. My husband trusted you.

280
00:22:17,950 --> 00:22:21,290
And you repaid our faith with treachery.

281
00:22:21,290 --> 00:22:22,500
- No, My Lady. - Get out!

282
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:23,630
Cat, I've...

283
00:22:24,980 --> 00:22:27,290
I've loved you since I was a boy.

284
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:31,540
It seems to me that fate has given us this chance...

285
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:33,990
Have you lost your mind? Get out!

286
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,490
Do you want to see your girls again?

287
00:22:52,710 --> 00:22:55,810
Sansa, more beautiful than ever.

288
00:22:56,210 --> 00:23:00,070
And Arya, just as wild as ever.

289
00:23:01,060 --> 00:23:02,610
You have Arya, too?

290
00:23:02,610 --> 00:23:07,080
Both girls are healthy and safe...

291
00:23:07,670 --> 00:23:09,140
for now.

292
00:23:09,750 --> 00:23:12,970
But you know the Queen and you know Joffrey.

293
00:23:14,090 --> 00:23:16,490
I fear for their longevity

294
00:23:16,490 --> 00:23:18,300
if they remain in the capital.

295
00:23:40,410 --> 00:23:42,050
What do you want?

296
00:23:43,590 --> 00:23:46,360
The Lannisters will trade your daughters for the Kingslayer.

297
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:47,960
Of course they will.

298
00:23:48,010 --> 00:23:50,690
Jaime Lannister for two girls?

299
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:52,890
Robb will never agree to those terms.

300
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:54,870
I'm not bringing these terms to him.

301
00:23:55,060 --> 00:23:56,870
I'm bringing them to you.

302
00:23:56,870 --> 00:23:59,330
You think I'd keep secrets from my son?

303
00:23:59,330 --> 00:24:02,180
Robb has surprised them all with his skills in battle,

304
00:24:02,180 --> 00:24:03,650
but he's not a mother.

305
00:24:04,330 --> 00:24:05,950
Consider it, Cat.

306
00:24:07,450 --> 00:24:09,540
You may not get another chance.

307
00:24:14,230 --> 00:24:16,880
- I've brought you a gift. - I don't want your gifts.

308
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:19,570
A token of Tyrion Lannister's goodwill.

309
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:24,400
He wants you to understand that this exchange of prisoners

310
00:24:25,260 --> 00:24:26,550
is offered in good faith.

311
00:24:26,550 --> 00:24:27,960
Good faith?

312
00:24:33,140 --> 00:24:34,520
What's this?

313
00:25:03,770 --> 00:25:06,000
Your husband was an honorable man.

314
00:25:06,970 --> 00:25:10,560
He should rest beside his family in the crypts beneath Winterfell.

315
00:25:14,940 --> 00:25:17,190
- You may not believe... - Get out.

316
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:53,620
Get up, you dogs.

317
00:26:03,590 --> 00:26:06,530
That's him, the one who picks.

318
00:26:07,790 --> 00:26:09,180
The Mountain.

319
00:26:11,930 --> 00:26:13,310
What are you doing?

320
00:26:13,870 --> 00:26:16,120
He told me he stares at him every day.

321
00:26:16,120 --> 00:26:17,770
That's why he doesn't get picked.

322
00:26:43,820 --> 00:26:45,050
You.

323
00:26:46,050 --> 00:26:47,320
Move, boy!

324
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:49,160
Move!

325
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:11,510
Is there gold and silver in the village?

326
00:27:11,510 --> 00:27:13,630
- I don't know. - Gems?

327
00:27:14,850 --> 00:27:16,200
I didn't see any.

328
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:18,680
- Where is the brotherhood? - I don't know.

329
00:27:34,730 --> 00:27:37,660
- Where is the brotherhood? - I don't know. Please.

330
00:27:37,660 --> 00:27:40,240
- Where is the brotherhood? - I don't know.

331
00:27:46,210 --> 00:27:47,960
Which of the villagers aided them?

332
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:49,880
- I don't know. - Who?

333
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:50,850
I...

334
00:27:55,450 --> 00:27:57,800
- Who? - I never saw.

335
00:27:57,800 --> 00:27:59,420
- Who? - I never saw.

336
00:27:59,420 --> 00:28:02,710
Please. Please, stop. Please, it's starting to...

337
00:28:02,710 --> 00:28:03,640
Who?

338
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:06,150
I didn't see anyone help him.

339
00:28:06,590 --> 00:28:08,280
Take it off! Take it off!

340
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:09,420
Who helped him?

341
00:28:09,420 --> 00:28:11,790
Ganes the butcher and his son.

342
00:28:11,790 --> 00:28:13,010
That's better.

343
00:28:13,010 --> 00:28:14,460
You've been very helpful.

344
00:28:14,460 --> 00:28:15,920
No, stop, please!

345
00:28:15,920 --> 00:28:18,360
What are you doing? Please, stop!

346
00:28:18,360 --> 00:28:21,020
Please, stop! No! No!

347
00:28:21,020 --> 00:28:23,150
I told you everything! No!

348
00:28:23,150 --> 00:28:25,110
No!

349
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:28,290
Joffrey.

350
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:31,280
Cersei.

351
00:28:31,950 --> 00:28:33,080
Ilyn Payne.

352
00:28:33,380 --> 00:28:34,510
The hound.

353
00:28:34,510 --> 00:28:37,580
Please, Polliver. Some food.

354
00:28:37,580 --> 00:28:39,590
Just a crust of bread.

355
00:28:44,020 --> 00:28:45,590
Polliver.

356
00:28:46,140 --> 00:28:47,470
The Mountain.

357
00:29:05,460 --> 00:29:08,450
Lady stark, I had not thought to find you in the Stormlands.

358
00:29:08,450 --> 00:29:11,520
I had not thought to be here, Lord Stannis.

359
00:29:12,330 --> 00:29:13,800
Can that truly be you?

360
00:29:13,800 --> 00:29:15,580
Who else might it be?

361
00:29:15,580 --> 00:29:18,120
When I saw your standard, I couldn't be sure.

362
00:29:18,820 --> 00:29:19,750
Whose banner is that?

363
00:29:19,750 --> 00:29:20,810
My own.

364
00:29:22,130 --> 00:29:23,380
I suppose if we used the same one,

365
00:29:23,380 --> 00:29:25,710
the battle would be terribly confusing.

366
00:29:26,080 --> 00:29:27,720
Why is your stag on fire?

367
00:29:29,430 --> 00:29:33,540
The king has taken for his sigil the fiery heart of the Lord of Light.

368
00:29:33,540 --> 00:29:38,120
Ah, you must be this fire priestess we hear so much about.

369
00:29:38,890 --> 00:29:40,200
Mm, brother,

370
00:29:40,630 --> 00:29:43,790
now I understand why you found religion in your old age.

371
00:29:43,790 --> 00:29:45,070
Watch yourself, Renly.

372
00:29:45,070 --> 00:29:46,830
No, no, I'm relieved.

373
00:29:47,890 --> 00:29:49,660
I never really believed you're a fanatic.

374
00:29:50,230 --> 00:29:53,580
Charmless, rigid, a bore, yes,

375
00:29:53,580 --> 00:29:55,330
but not a godly man.

376
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:57,320
You should kneel before your brother.

377
00:29:57,840 --> 00:29:59,310
He's the Lord's chosen,

378
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:02,370
born amidst salt and smoke.

379
00:30:02,370 --> 00:30:04,560
Born amidst salt and smoke?

380
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:06,210
Is he a ham?

381
00:30:06,210 --> 00:30:07,860
That's twice I've warned you.

382
00:30:07,860 --> 00:30:09,420
Listen to yourselves.

383
00:30:09,890 --> 00:30:11,200
If you were sons of mine,

384
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:13,970
I would knock your heads together and lock you in a bedchamber

385
00:30:13,970 --> 00:30:16,410
until you remembered that you were brothers.

386
00:30:16,410 --> 00:30:19,170
It is strange to find you beside my brother, Lady Stark.

387
00:30:19,670 --> 00:30:21,920
Your husband was a supporter of my claim.

388
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:24,380
Lord Eddard's integrity cost him his head.

389
00:30:24,380 --> 00:30:27,050
And you sit beside this pretender and chastise me.

390
00:30:27,050 --> 00:30:28,850
We share a common enemy.

391
00:30:28,850 --> 00:30:31,900
The iron throne is mine by right.

392
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:35,180
All those that deny that are my foes.

393
00:30:36,500 --> 00:30:39,130
The whole realm denies it, from Dorne to the Wall.

394
00:30:39,130 --> 00:30:41,130
Old men deny it with their death rattle

395
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:44,000
and unborn children deny it in their mother's wombs.

396
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:48,080
No one wants you for their king.

397
00:30:48,620 --> 00:30:50,700
You never wanted any friends, brother.

398
00:30:51,100 --> 00:30:53,970
But a man without friends is a man without power.

399
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:57,060
For the sake of the mother who bore us,

400
00:30:57,660 --> 00:31:00,270
I will give you this one night to reconsider.

401
00:31:00,620 --> 00:31:02,100
Strike your banners,

402
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:04,380
come to me before dawn,

403
00:31:05,020 --> 00:31:07,930
and I will grant you your old seat in the council.

404
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:11,130
I'll even name you my heir

405
00:31:12,310 --> 00:31:14,070
until a son is born to me.

406
00:31:15,700 --> 00:31:17,530
Otherwise I shall destroy you.

407
00:31:22,020 --> 00:31:23,680
Look across those fields, brother.

408
00:31:24,970 --> 00:31:26,460
Can you see all those banners?

409
00:31:26,460 --> 00:31:28,990
You think a few bolts of cloth will make you king?

410
00:31:28,990 --> 00:31:29,850
No.

411
00:31:31,520 --> 00:31:34,160
The men holding those bolts of cloth will make me king.

412
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:36,510
We shall see, Renly.

413
00:31:36,510 --> 00:31:38,930
Come the dawn, we shall see.

414
00:31:39,370 --> 00:31:41,480
Look to your sins, Lord Renly.

415
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:43,980
The night is dark and full of terrors.

416
00:31:49,750 --> 00:31:52,950
Would you believe I loved him once?

417
00:32:13,510 --> 00:32:14,850
I thought we were welcome.

418
00:32:15,670 --> 00:32:18,380
If you heard a Dothraki horde was approaching your city,

419
00:32:18,380 --> 00:32:20,190
you might do the same, Khaleesi.

420
00:32:22,970 --> 00:32:24,130
Horde?

421
00:32:39,500 --> 00:32:42,140
My name is Daenerys...

422
00:32:42,140 --> 00:32:44,540
Daenerys stormborn of the House Targaryen.

423
00:32:45,250 --> 00:32:46,740
You know me, My Lord?

424
00:32:46,740 --> 00:32:49,160
Only by reputation, Khaleesi.

425
00:32:49,160 --> 00:32:52,260
And I'm no lord, merely a humble merchant.

426
00:32:54,260 --> 00:32:56,810
They call you the Mother of Dragons.

427
00:32:56,810 --> 00:32:58,630
And what should I call you?

428
00:32:59,100 --> 00:33:00,470
Oh, my name is quite long

429
00:33:00,470 --> 00:33:03,200
and quite impossible for foreigners to pronounce.

430
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:06,500
I am simply a trader of spices.

431
00:33:06,830 --> 00:33:10,150
But we are The Thirteen,

432
00:33:10,150 --> 00:33:13,570
charged with the governance and protection of Qarth,

433
00:33:13,570 --> 00:33:16,670
the greatest city that ever was or will be.

434
00:33:18,170 --> 00:33:21,870
- The beauty of Quarth is legendary-- - Qarth.

435
00:33:24,430 --> 00:33:25,570
Qarth.

436
00:33:26,360 --> 00:33:28,150
Might we see the dragons?

437
00:33:33,770 --> 00:33:36,760
My friend,

438
00:33:37,470 --> 00:33:39,440
we have travelled very far.

439
00:33:39,850 --> 00:33:42,140
We have no food, no water.

440
00:33:42,140 --> 00:33:44,820
Once I see my people fed, I would be honored--

441
00:33:44,820 --> 00:33:47,650
Forgive me, Mother of Dragons,

442
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:51,360
but no man alive has seen a living dragon.

443
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:55,300
Some of my more skeptical friends refuse to believe

444
00:33:55,300 --> 00:33:59,120
your children even exist.

445
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:02,380
All we ask is the chance to see for ourselves.

446
00:34:03,350 --> 00:34:04,730
I am not a liar.

447
00:34:04,730 --> 00:34:06,310
Oh, I don't think you are.

448
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:08,330
But as I've never met you before,

449
00:34:08,330 --> 00:34:11,250
my opinion on the matter is of limited value.

450
00:34:13,140 --> 00:34:15,020
Where I come from,

451
00:34:15,820 --> 00:34:18,280
guests are treated with respect,

452
00:34:18,280 --> 00:34:21,060
not insulted at the gates.

453
00:34:21,060 --> 00:34:23,890
Then perhaps you should return to where you come from.

454
00:34:24,350 --> 00:34:25,740
We wish you well.

455
00:34:29,860 --> 00:34:31,300
What are you doing?

456
00:34:31,870 --> 00:34:34,220
You promised to receive me.

457
00:34:35,560 --> 00:34:37,020
We have received you.

458
00:34:37,020 --> 00:34:39,910
Here we are, and here you are.

459
00:34:39,910 --> 00:34:43,650
If you do not let us in, all of us will die.

460
00:34:43,650 --> 00:34:46,380
Which we shall deeply regret.

461
00:34:46,380 --> 00:34:49,520
But Qarth did not become the greatest city that ever was or will be

462
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:53,360
by letting Dothraki savages through its gates.

463
00:34:59,820 --> 00:35:02,360
Khaleesi, please be careful.

464
00:35:05,290 --> 00:35:06,720
Thirteen!

465
00:35:08,120 --> 00:35:10,460
When my dragons are grown,

466
00:35:10,580 --> 00:35:13,650
we will take back what was stolen from me

467
00:35:13,650 --> 00:35:15,960
and destroy those who have wronged me.

468
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:20,880
We will lay waste to armies and burn cities to the ground.

469
00:35:21,250 --> 00:35:25,480
Turn us away and we will burn you first.

470
00:35:28,010 --> 00:35:30,800
You are a true Targaryen.

471
00:35:31,720 --> 00:35:33,230
Only, as you said a moment ago,

472
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:35,050
if we don't let you into the city,

473
00:35:35,100 --> 00:35:37,030
you will all die. And so...

474
00:35:37,180 --> 00:35:39,710
Retreating in fear from a little girl

475
00:35:39,710 --> 00:35:43,770
is unbecoming of the greatest city that ever was or will be.

476
00:35:43,970 --> 00:35:47,500
The discussion is over, Xaro Xhoan Daxos.

477
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:49,510
The Thirteen have spoken.

478
00:35:49,510 --> 00:35:52,030
I am one of the Thirteen

479
00:35:52,540 --> 00:35:54,290
and I am still speaking.

480
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:57,130
The girl threatens to burn our city to the ground

481
00:35:57,130 --> 00:35:59,920
and you would invite her in for a cup of wine?

482
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:02,000
She is the Mother of Dragons.

483
00:36:02,820 --> 00:36:05,570
Do you expect her to watch her people starve

484
00:36:06,050 --> 00:36:07,650
without breathing fire?

485
00:36:08,110 --> 00:36:10,490
I believe we can allow a few Dothraki

486
00:36:10,490 --> 00:36:13,130
through our gates without dooming our city.

487
00:36:13,130 --> 00:36:15,680
After all, here I am,

488
00:36:16,380 --> 00:36:18,600
a savage from the Summer Isles,

489
00:36:18,600 --> 00:36:20,430
and Qarth still stands.

490
00:36:20,990 --> 00:36:22,590
Our decision is final.

491
00:36:23,760 --> 00:36:24,760
Very well.

492
00:36:28,010 --> 00:36:29,880
I invoke Soumai.

493
00:36:34,560 --> 00:36:37,090
I will vouch for her, her people,

494
00:36:37,090 --> 00:36:40,300
and her dragons in accordance with the law.

495
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:48,180
Be it on your head.

496
00:36:50,160 --> 00:36:52,500
Welcome to Qarth, My Lady.

497
00:37:42,330 --> 00:37:43,510
You.

498
00:37:53,370 --> 00:37:55,710
Is there gold or silver in the village?

499
00:37:55,710 --> 00:37:56,920
I'm not from the village.

500
00:37:56,920 --> 00:37:58,440
Where is the brotherhood?

501
00:37:59,750 --> 00:38:01,220
I don't know what that is.

502
00:38:30,420 --> 00:38:34,560
You two, take Lord Lannister's things to his quarters.

503
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:35,990
What's this?

504
00:38:35,990 --> 00:38:39,020
We weren't expecting you till tomorrow, Lord Tywin.

505
00:38:40,090 --> 00:38:41,550
Evidently not.

506
00:38:43,790 --> 00:38:45,340
Why are these prisoners not in their cells?

507
00:38:45,340 --> 00:38:47,720
Cells are overflowing, My Lord.

508
00:38:48,050 --> 00:38:49,610
This lot won't be here long.

509
00:38:50,080 --> 00:38:51,900
Don't need no permanent place.

510
00:38:52,110 --> 00:38:54,470
After we interrogate 'em, we usually just...

511
00:38:55,460 --> 00:38:57,110
Are we so well-manned

512
00:38:57,470 --> 00:39:02,280
that we can afford to discard able young bodies and skilled laborers?

513
00:39:11,740 --> 00:39:14,390
You, do you have a trade?

514
00:39:15,910 --> 00:39:17,240
Smith, My Lord.

515
00:39:19,280 --> 00:39:21,330
What are you looking at? Kneel!

516
00:39:22,640 --> 00:39:25,950
Kneel or I'll carve your lungs out, boy.

517
00:39:26,140 --> 00:39:27,760
He'll do no such thing.

518
00:39:28,850 --> 00:39:31,490
This one's a girl, you idiot,

519
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:34,770
Dressed as a boy. why?

520
00:39:34,770 --> 00:39:36,560
Safer to travel, My Lord.

521
00:39:37,210 --> 00:39:38,410
Smart.

522
00:39:39,060 --> 00:39:40,950
More than I can say for this lot.

523
00:39:40,950 --> 00:39:42,990
Get these prisoners to work.

524
00:39:43,790 --> 00:39:45,080
Bring the girl.

525
00:39:46,160 --> 00:39:48,270
- I need a new cupbearer. - My Lord.

526
00:39:56,580 --> 00:39:58,600
Your visits are too few, cousin.

527
00:39:58,600 --> 00:39:59,980
Her Grace, the queen regent,

528
00:39:59,980 --> 00:40:02,690
commands you to release Grand Maester Pycelle.

529
00:40:02,690 --> 00:40:04,010
Here's your warrant.

530
00:40:04,010 --> 00:40:05,180
So it is.

531
00:40:05,750 --> 00:40:07,870
Will you take a cup with me?

532
00:40:08,220 --> 00:40:10,890
I find that mulled wine helps me sleep.

533
00:40:10,890 --> 00:40:12,720
I am here at Her Grace's behest,

534
00:40:12,720 --> 00:40:14,470
not to drink with you, Imp.

535
00:40:15,380 --> 00:40:18,250
If my sister was so concerned for Pycelle,

536
00:40:18,250 --> 00:40:20,270
I would have thought she'd come herself.

537
00:40:20,270 --> 00:40:21,920
Instead she sends you.

538
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:23,550
What am I to make of that?

539
00:40:23,550 --> 00:40:25,270
I don't care what you make of it,

540
00:40:25,270 --> 00:40:27,970
so long as you release your prisoner immediately.

541
00:40:27,970 --> 00:40:31,600
And you've received these instructions directly from Cersei?

542
00:40:32,290 --> 00:40:34,170
As I said several times.

543
00:40:34,170 --> 00:40:37,130
And you've waited this long to deliver the information?

544
00:40:37,770 --> 00:40:39,210
When the queen regent gives me a command,

545
00:40:39,210 --> 00:40:40,860
I carry it out without delay.

546
00:40:43,820 --> 00:40:47,150
Cersei must have great trust in you,

547
00:40:47,150 --> 00:40:51,130
allowing you into her chamber during the hour of the wolf.

548
00:40:55,750 --> 00:40:58,220
The queen regent has a great many responsibilities.

549
00:40:58,220 --> 00:40:59,770
She often works from dusk till dawn.

550
00:40:59,770 --> 00:41:02,390
She must be very glad to have you helping her

551
00:41:02,390 --> 00:41:04,280
from dusk till dawn.

552
00:41:05,780 --> 00:41:08,120
Ah, lavender oil.

553
00:41:08,120 --> 00:41:10,650
She always loved lavender oil, even as a girl.

554
00:41:10,650 --> 00:41:12,140
I am a knight!

555
00:41:12,810 --> 00:41:14,850
An anointed knight, yes.

556
00:41:14,850 --> 00:41:17,380
Tell me, did Cersei have you knighted

557
00:41:17,380 --> 00:41:20,220
before or after she took you into her bed?

558
00:41:21,310 --> 00:41:23,910
What? Nothing to say?

559
00:41:23,910 --> 00:41:25,880
No more warnings for me, Ser?

560
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:27,530
You will withdraw these filthy accusations.

561
00:41:27,530 --> 00:41:29,310
Have you ever given any thought

562
00:41:29,310 --> 00:41:31,240
to what king Joffrey will have to say

563
00:41:31,240 --> 00:41:33,720
when he finds out you've been bedding his mother?

564
00:41:38,680 --> 00:41:39,860
It's not my fault!

565
00:41:39,860 --> 00:41:42,820
Did she take you against your will?

566
00:41:42,820 --> 00:41:44,630
Can you not defend yourself, knight?

567
00:41:44,630 --> 00:41:48,010
Your own father, Lord Tywin, when I was named the king's squire,

568
00:41:48,010 --> 00:41:50,150
he told me to obey her in everything.

569
00:41:50,150 --> 00:41:52,040
Did he tell you to fuck her, too?

570
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:55,310
I only meant I did as I was bid.

571
00:41:55,310 --> 00:41:57,090
Hated every moment of it,

572
00:41:57,090 --> 00:41:59,070
is that what you'll have me believe?

573
00:41:59,070 --> 00:42:01,100
A high place in court, a knighthood,

574
00:42:01,100 --> 00:42:03,490
my sister's legs spreading open for you at night.

575
00:42:03,490 --> 00:42:05,910
Oh, yes, it must have been terrible.

576
00:42:05,910 --> 00:42:07,960
Wait here. His Grace will want to hear this.

577
00:42:07,960 --> 00:42:09,750
Mercy! Mercy, My Lord! I beg you.

578
00:42:09,750 --> 00:42:12,090
Save it for Joffrey. He loves a good grovel.

579
00:42:12,090 --> 00:42:14,550
My Lord, it was your sister's bidding... the Queen.

580
00:42:14,550 --> 00:42:16,310
I'll leave the city at once, I swear.

581
00:42:16,310 --> 00:42:18,320
No, I think not.

582
00:42:18,770 --> 00:42:19,950
My Lord?

583
00:42:20,540 --> 00:42:21,940
You heard me.

584
00:42:25,210 --> 00:42:27,820
My father told you to obey my sister. Obey her.

585
00:42:28,500 --> 00:42:31,280
Stay close to her side. Keep her trust.

586
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:33,580
Pleasure her whenever she requires.

587
00:42:33,840 --> 00:42:35,380
No one ever need know

588
00:42:36,150 --> 00:42:38,880
as long as you keep faith with me.

589
00:42:40,550 --> 00:42:42,860
I want to know what Cersei is doing,

590
00:42:42,860 --> 00:42:45,780
where she goes, who she sees,

591
00:42:45,780 --> 00:42:48,070
what they talk of... everything.

592
00:42:48,910 --> 00:42:50,350
And you will tell me.

593
00:42:51,190 --> 00:42:52,790
Yes, My Lord, I will.

594
00:42:53,160 --> 00:42:54,760
I swear it, as you command.

595
00:42:57,840 --> 00:43:00,220
Oh, rise, rise.

596
00:43:00,900 --> 00:43:03,190
Let us drink to our understanding.

597
00:43:03,610 --> 00:43:06,020
Oh, you don't have a cup. Oh, well.

598
00:43:06,730 --> 00:43:09,660
Smile, cousin. My sister is a beautiful woman.

599
00:43:09,660 --> 00:43:11,060
And it's all for the good of the realm.

600
00:43:11,060 --> 00:43:13,680
Go back and tell her that I beg her forgiveness,

601
00:43:13,680 --> 00:43:15,900
that I want no more conflict between us

602
00:43:15,900 --> 00:43:19,350
and that henceforth I shall do nothing without her consent.

603
00:43:19,350 --> 00:43:20,770
But her demands.

604
00:43:21,160 --> 00:43:23,490
Oh, I'll give her Pycelle.

605
00:43:24,090 --> 00:43:25,940
- You will? - Yes, I'll release him in the morning.

606
00:43:25,940 --> 00:43:27,500
Cersei can keep him as a pet if she wants,

607
00:43:27,500 --> 00:43:29,380
but I will not have him on the Council.

608
00:43:29,790 --> 00:43:32,660
I could swear that I had not harmed a single hair on his head,

609
00:43:32,660 --> 00:43:36,040
but that would not, strictly speaking, be true.

610
00:43:46,980 --> 00:43:50,240
Stay within one table length.

611
00:43:55,280 --> 00:43:56,400
Your Grace.

612
00:44:02,100 --> 00:44:04,020
Do your knucklebones bring you luck?

613
00:44:07,310 --> 00:44:09,880
Well, life's been good since you hacked them off, Your Grace.

614
00:44:10,690 --> 00:44:12,780
And it's four less fingernails to clean.

615
00:44:12,780 --> 00:44:13,700
Fewer.

616
00:44:14,070 --> 00:44:15,090
Pardon?

617
00:44:16,220 --> 00:44:18,620
Four fewer fingernails to clean.

618
00:44:18,940 --> 00:44:21,070
Never understood why you had to wear them.

619
00:44:22,120 --> 00:44:24,410
It reminds me of where I come from and where I am now.

620
00:44:26,020 --> 00:44:27,560
It reminds me of your justice.

621
00:44:27,560 --> 00:44:29,090
It was an honest punishment

622
00:44:29,090 --> 00:44:30,400
and you were good with the cleaver.

623
00:44:30,400 --> 00:44:32,290
You were a hero and a smuggler.

624
00:44:34,520 --> 00:44:36,820
A good act does not wash out the bad,

625
00:44:37,110 --> 00:44:38,850
nor a bad the good.

626
00:44:39,890 --> 00:44:41,910
A lesson I've tried to teach my son.

627
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:45,680
- Does he listen? - To me? Gods, no.

628
00:44:47,360 --> 00:44:50,050
But if your red woman told him to leap from the Crow's Nest...

629
00:44:50,050 --> 00:44:51,340
She has a name.

630
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:57,460
I trust you've not forgotten your smuggler's tricks.

631
00:45:00,300 --> 00:45:01,970
I've lived within the law for 17--

632
00:45:01,970 --> 00:45:04,220
I want you to be a smuggler this time.

633
00:45:05,340 --> 00:45:06,710
Any shore, any night.

634
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:08,830
What am I bringing ashore?

635
00:45:08,830 --> 00:45:10,090
The red woman.

636
00:45:12,350 --> 00:45:14,100
No one must know what you do

637
00:45:14,750 --> 00:45:16,110
and we'll not speak of this again.

638
00:45:16,110 --> 00:45:19,690
I am true to Your Grace and always will be,

639
00:45:20,270 --> 00:45:22,870
but surely there are other ways, cleaner ways.

640
00:45:22,870 --> 00:45:24,880
Cleaner ways don't win wars.

641
00:45:55,020 --> 00:45:57,350
Are you afraid, Onion Knight?

642
00:46:00,460 --> 00:46:04,180
Someone once told me the night is dark and full of terrors.

643
00:46:05,540 --> 00:46:08,000
You've carried more unpleasant cargo in your time.

644
00:46:12,440 --> 00:46:15,290
Are you a good man, ser Davos Seaworth?

645
00:46:15,290 --> 00:46:18,150
I'd say my parts are mixed, My Lady--

646
00:46:18,150 --> 00:46:19,220
good and bad.

647
00:46:19,650 --> 00:46:21,580
If half an onion is black with rot,

648
00:46:21,580 --> 00:46:22,800
it's a rotten onion.

649
00:46:23,740 --> 00:46:25,700
A man is good or he is evil.

650
00:46:26,040 --> 00:46:27,310
And which are you?

651
00:46:27,310 --> 00:46:28,530
Oh, good.

652
00:46:29,140 --> 00:46:31,200
I'm a knight myself of sorts,

653
00:46:31,770 --> 00:46:33,830
a champion of light and life.

654
00:46:35,520 --> 00:46:37,260
Well, that must be very nice for you.

655
00:46:54,270 --> 00:46:55,960
Do you love your wife?

656
00:46:56,670 --> 00:46:57,650
I do.

657
00:46:58,160 --> 00:47:00,010
Yet you have known other women.

658
00:47:00,430 --> 00:47:02,010
Don't talk about my wife.

659
00:47:02,010 --> 00:47:05,170
I'm not. I'm talking about other women.

660
00:47:06,340 --> 00:47:08,260
Like me, ser Davos.

661
00:47:12,790 --> 00:47:14,410
You want me.

662
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:17,420
You want to see what's beneath this robe.

663
00:47:19,940 --> 00:47:21,520
And you will.

664
00:47:26,200 --> 00:47:28,980
Strange that this Lord of Light

665
00:47:29,370 --> 00:47:31,300
asks you to work in the shadows.

666
00:47:32,460 --> 00:47:35,160
Shadows cannot live in the dark, ser Davos.

667
00:47:35,510 --> 00:47:37,250
They are servants of light,

668
00:47:37,900 --> 00:47:39,720
the children of fire.

669
00:47:40,570 --> 00:47:44,030
And the brighter the flame, the darker they are.

670
00:47:44,030 --> 00:47:46,520
These weren't here before. They've barred the passage.

671
00:47:47,930 --> 00:47:50,020
They can't bar our passage.

672
00:47:55,190 --> 00:47:56,930
Gods protect us.

673
00:47:57,370 --> 00:48:00,100
There's only one god, ser Davos,

674
00:48:00,990 --> 00:48:04,080
and he only protects those who serve him.

